1. Add a missing theorem item, e.g. PAPER-BURUNGALE-TIAN-26/cm-characterization, with this statement: "Let f ∈ S_k(Γ1(N)) be a normalized newform with k≥2. The following are equivalent:
   (a) f has a nontrivial self-twist in the sense of ModularForms Layer 9, i.e. f = primitive(f⊗χ) with χ≠1;
   (b) f has CM in Kato's sense (Remark 12.8): there are an imaginary quadratic K and a continuous Hecke character ψ with L(f,s)=L(ψ,s);
   (c) f is the newform θ_ψ attached to an algebraic Hecke character ψ of an imaginary quadratic K of infinity type (1−k,0).
   In that case χ=ε_K and K is imaginary quadratic. In (b), ψ may be replaced by ψ∘c so that it has type (1−k,0), and its conductor f_ψ satisfies N=|d_K|·N(f_ψ), with the nebentypus determined by ψ and ε_K."
   Locator: BT §2.2.5, p.5; Kato Remark 12.8 (p.223) and 15.10 (p.260); source Ribet, LNM 601 (1977), 17–52 (Kato's [Ri2]).
2. Route the item once. Either add it as a source item to GL2AutomorphicRepresentationsAndTransfer R17.5, importing R17.4's cuspidality criterion, R16.6 and AutomorphicFormsOnReductiveGroups AF.5; or put it in route 7 (CMAllPrimeMainConjectures) ahead of cm-kato-main. In either case import the Layer 9 self-twist predicate rather than defining a second one.
3. In cm-newform's note, say three things:
   - the definition is the image of automorphic induction;
   - R17.5 and R16.6 plan only the direction from ψ to f;
   - its agreement with Kato's hypothesis and with the Layer 9 CM predicate is the new item.
